      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad newcomer",
          "heading": "Jamie Benson reveals Farrell called him into Ireland training before Ulster move",
          "body": "Ulster's Jamie Benson, 24, calls the call-up a shock. Farrell brought him into training in July, before he had set foot in Ulster after leaving Harlequins. “Obviously, it was a bit of a shock to be called in here before I’d even set foot in Ulster, but it was a great feeling,” Benson says. His mother Carole, who grew up in Belfast, was delighted, though she was careful not to push him towards Ireland, and he is now in the Ireland squad."
