          "heading": "Wales release Josh Adams to play for Cardiff in Welsh derby",
          "body": "The 31-year-old has played just twice this season, so Wales let him go back to Cardiff for the Ospreys match to get more game time. Adams was a regular for Wales last year, starting two autumn Tests and every Six Nations game, and returned to action earlier this month. Meanwhile Tom Rogers, Dan Edwards, Reuben Morgan-Williams and Gareth Thomas were in Wales camp preparing for the Japan Test."
